invalid `start` value (e.g., `start=0`). The validation order causes the method 
to convert `end=-1` to `None` before validating that `start=0` is invalid, 
resulting in misleading error messages.\n\n## Lens\n**Phase 1: The Intent vs. 
Reality Check** - Logic Gaps in validation order\n\n## Expected vs. Observed\n| 
Expected Behavior | Observed Risk |\n|---|---|\n| When `start=0` (invalid) and 
`end=-1` (valid special case), method should immediately return error about 
invalid `start` value | Method converts `end=-1` to `None` first, then validates
line range `start > end` where `end=None`, which doesn\'t trigger the invalid 
range check, allowing execution to continue with confusing error messages |\n| 
Invalid line number validation should happen before any special case handling of
`end=-1` | Special case handling of `end=-1` happens before complete validation,
potentially masking real validation errors |\n\n## Root Cause\nIn the 
`should_read_file` method (lines 525-545), the validation logic has this 
order:\n1. Validate `start` if provided (rejects non-int, negative, zero)\n2. 
Validate `end` if provided (rejects non-int, negative except -1)\n3. Convert 
`end=-1` to `None` (special case for "read to EOF")\n4. Validate line range if 
both `start` and `end` are not `None` and `start > end`\n\nThe bug occurs at 
step 3: when `start=0` (invalid) and `end=-1` (valid special case), step 3 
converts `end=-1` to `None`, then step 4\'s check `if start is not None and end 
is not None and end != -1 and start > end:` evaluates to `False` because 
`end=None`. The invalid `start=0` passes the initial check (`start < 1`), but 
then the method continues execution instead of returning an error 
immediately.\n\n## Fix Plan\nChange the validation order to:\n1. Validate 
`start` if provided (rejects non-int, values < 1)\n2. Validate `end` if provided
(rejects non-int, values < 1 except -1)\n3. **Immediately return error if 
validation fails** (don\'t proceed to special case handling)\n4. Only after 
validation passes, handle special case `end=-1` → `None`\n5. Validate line range
ordering\n\n## Status: IN PROGRESS'})
