Four Lenses Bug Report: src/henchman/agents/working_memory.py\n## Date: 
2025-03-16T16:00:00Z\n## Bug Summary\nThe `should_read_file` method has a 
misleading error message bug. When `start=None, end=None` (read entire file) and
the file has some recorded line ranges (`valid_ranges` not empty), the method 
returns `True` with reason "File not fully read - partial read recorded". This 
message is incorrect because:\n1. We don\'t know if the file was "not fully 
read" (we don\'t know file size)\n2. "partial read recorded" implies we know it 
was a partial read, but we only know some lines were read, not whether all lines
were read\n\nThe message should be more accurate, e.g., "File may not be fully 
read - cannot determine without file size" or "Cannot verify file fully read 
based on recorded ranges".\n\n## Lens\n**Phase 1: The Intent vs. Reality Check**
- Logic Gaps (incorrect assumptions in error messages)\n\n## Expected vs. 
Observed\n| Expected Behavior | Observed Risk |\n|---|---|\n| Error messages 
should accurately reflect what we know vs. assume | Message assumes file wasn\'t
fully read when we only know some lines were read |\n| When we can\'t determine 
if file needs reading (due to missing info), message should say so | Message 
states incorrect fact ("not fully read") as if it\'s known |\n| Conservative 
approach (return `True` when unsure) is correct, but message should match | 
Correct conservative behavior with incorrect justification |\n\n## Root 
Cause\n1. **Incorrect assumption in error message**: The code assumes 
`valid_ranges` not empty means "file wasn\'t read fully". Actually, it means 
"some lines were read (could be all or some)".\n2. **Missing nuance**: Without 
file size information, we can\'t determine if recorded ranges cover the entire 
file. The error message doesn\'t reflect this uncertainty.\n3. **Comment 
reinforces incorrect assumption**: The comment says "Want to read entire file, 
but file wasn\'t read fully" which is the same incorrect assumption.\n\n## Fix 
Plan\n1. Change the error message from "File not fully read - partial read 
recorded" to "Cannot determine if file fully read - some lines recorded but file
size unknown" or similar.\n2. Update the comment to reflect the uncertainty.\n3.
Keep the conservative behavior (return `True` when unsure if file was fully 
read).\n\n## Status: FIXED\n\n## Files Changed\n1. 
`src/henchman/agents/working_memory.py` (lines 606-609):\n   - Changed error 
